1
00:00:00.750 --> 00:00:06.675
P2.2 · Working capital: DSO, DPO, DIO and trailing windows

2
00:00:07.825 --> 00:00:13.443
DSO, DPO and DIO estimate days to collect, to sell stock, and to pay.

3
00:00:13.493 --> 00:00:18.284
The cash conversion cycle is DSO plus DIO minus DPO.

4
00:00:19.434 --> 00:00:23.996
Here, DSO is 86 days, against a benchmark of 42.

5
00:00:24.046 --> 00:00:30.774
K-φ uses a three-month trailing window by default: a single month can mislead in either direction.

6
00:00:31.924 --> 00:00:36.602
Below, receivables by customer, with each one's terms and actual days.

7
00:00:36.652 --> 00:00:39.864
This is where you find which customer moved the DSO.

8
00:00:41.014 --> 00:00:46.062
DSO is a pointer. When it moves, open the receivables by customer.

